  "summary": "Remote volcanic sub-Antarctic islands in the southern Indian Ocean, now an uninhabited Australian external territory. First confirmed sighted in 1853, with the first recorded landing in 1855. Australia ran a research station there from 1947 to 1955, and the islands were inscribed on the World Heritage List in 1997.",
